# L §4.6 step 1 (round 8b): a row's span is tested at the period of x's time key only when x is an input keyed by one
# period index; a rule, a band, and an input keyed by no period index or by more than one, are tested at the law date
# d (§4.3). wscale, a def keyed by two month indexes, is read at its law date start_of(c): w1 = 1 (rule fixed, d ==
# fixed); w2 = cpi_used[2026] / cpi_used[2025] = 104 / 100 = 1.04 (rule rebased). r, an input keyed by a month and
# a year index, is tested at the law date: its row governs 2026, so it gives 7 at law 2026-06-30 and has no
# candidate at 2027-06-30, HOLE-UNGOVERNED with the no-time-key question 'x at k: no value at <law date>' (step 5).
# (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §4.6: keyed by more than one time index.)
=== m.tally
model p15
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

source s "synthetic"

index mon = month 2026-01..2027-12
index yrs = year 2025..2027
index wd = [fixed, indexed]

input cpi_used[y in yrs]: num
input r[m in mon, y in yrs]: int

def wscale[c in mon, d in wd, m in mon]: num at start_of(c)
  rule fixed = 1 when d == fixed
  rule rebased = cpi_used[year_of(m) - 1] / cpi_used[year_of(c) - 1] when d == indexed

ask w1: wscale[2026-03, fixed, 2027-02]
ask w2: wscale[2026-03, indexed, 2027-02]
ask r1: r[2026-01, 2026] law 2026-06-30
ask r2: r[2026-01, 2026] law 2027-06-30

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  cpi_used[2025] = 100
  cpi_used[2026] = 104

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026
  known 2026-01-01
  r[2026-01, 2026] = 7
=== expect
r1: 7
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-10-18
r2: ?"r at 2026-01, 2026: no value at 2027-06-30" (r[2026-01, 2026])
  law date 2027-06-30, cut 2026-10-18
w1: 1
  cut 2026-10-18
w2: 1.04
  cut 2026-10-18
